**Intent:** Deliver what the pool holds into panes through the seam, gated on the receiver being idle (D7, D9 delivery half, D10, D13, D14, D15, D16, D19).
`Scheduler` runs one worker per receiver with pending deliveries (queued injects, or unread mail not muted by a hold or the orch rule), at most one delivery in flight per receiver, so a receiver whose sends stay busy delays no other; it subscribes to card 7's per-receiver wake notification to start or wake a worker.
At start it launches a worker for every receiver the rebuilt pool shows with a queued inject or unread mail not muted, so delivery after a daemon restart does not wait for a new post.
A worker wakes from a 1-second base and doubles its wait to an 8-second ceiling after every wake that delivers nothing (the receiver reads busy, held, paused or dormant, or reads idle while its reminder waits out the backoff), and returns to the base on any wake notification (a new post, reply, forward, inject or release) or on a wake that delivers; this departs from D19's list of busy, held or paused, since a dormant receiver or one inside its reminder backoff keeps a worker for hours and each wake spawns git and tmux through card 13's `Strands`, and `PATTERN-daemon-wakeups`' backoff rule wins; a receiver with nothing pending is not probed.
A probe for a dead or dormant receiver sends nothing and keeps its mail and queue; delivery resumes when `Strands` reports it live.
While `Delivery.Paused` covers the receiver nothing is typed, injects and reminders alike (D14).
An `Idle` or `Paused` error types nothing for that probe, is logged at Warn once per change of error, counts as a wake that delivers nothing and is retried at the next probe.
Nothing is ever typed into an orch strand (`agentname.MatchesRole` on `orch`, so `orch-N` included): an orch gets no worker and no `Idle` probe, and its reminders are journaled as one `withheld` event naming `creel-notices` per change of its unread set (a post, reply, forward or return to it), written by the verb or sweep that made the change rather than by a worker (D16); card 7's post, reply and forward write theirs, and the sweep's return writes its own.
Injects go first, in queue order: the worker appends and syncs `sending`, then calls `Send`; `nil` journals `injected`, `ErrBusy` retries at the next probe, `ErrNotLanded` journals `unconfirmed` and the inject is never retyped; another error is logged at Warn once per change of error and retried.
`inject --interrupt`'s queued head is typed at the next idle after `Interrupt` ran.
An inject's TTL runs only while the receiver is live and unpaused; a hold does not stop it, so an inject a hold mutes past its TTL expires; one still queued at expiry is journaled `expired` and never typed.
The consumed TTL is persisted as an `aged` event when the receiver turns live, dormant, paused or unpaused, every minute while the TTL runs, and when the scheduler stops.
`reminder.go` composes the reminder fresh from the unread set at delivery: `[creel] 2 unread: #41 from ly:x:driver «subject», #42 … — run lyx creel read`, at most 5 messages listed and the rest counted; a subject is cut to 80 runes with control characters and `«`/`»` replaced by spaces.
A reminder goes out at each busy-to-idle edge, except the first idle edge after creel's own reminder while the unread set is unchanged: then the next waits a backoff of 5 minutes, doubling to a 1-hour ceiling, reset by any change of the unread set.
A program sender's mailbox is never reminded.
While a hold covers the receiver, other senders' injects wait and their mail is not reminded; the hold owner's injects pass and its own unread mail is reminded alone; a hold ends at its expiry.
`sweep.go` (D15): while unread mail or a queued inject exists, a sweep lists strands from a 30-second base, doubling to a named 4-minute ceiling constant while two consecutive successful sweeps see the same strand-name set, and returning to the base on a change of that set, a new post, a new inject or a failed sweep; this departs from D15's fixed 30 seconds, since each sweep spawns git and tmux through card 13's `Strands` and an orch's withheld mail can keep it running for the daemon's life, and `PATTERN-daemon-wakeups`' backoff rule wins; a holder that is a strand name absent from two consecutive successful sweeps is gone; each unread message it holds goes one step back along its `Path` (the last forwarder, else `From`), journaled `returned` with the receiver that ended unread, and is reminded there; when that step is gone too it goes on toward the sender; when the sender is gone, EXTERNAL or a program, it is journaled `undelivered` and a `--wait-reply` waiter on it is answered returned-undelivered through card 7's waiter registry; each inject queued for a gone receiver is journaled `expired`, answering its `--wait` through the same registry.
A sweep whose `Strands` call fails moves nothing and counts toward no streak, and a strand removed and re-added between sweeps keeps its mail.
Bound: an agent that never reads costs one reminder turn per backoff step at most.
`internal/creelengine/deliver.go` and `internal/creelengine/sweep.go` join `cmd/lyx#unboundedWaitFiles`, and `pattern/PATTERN-daemon-wakeups.md`'s What-counts list gains creel's delivery workers (from 1 second, doubling to 8 seconds after every wake that delivers nothing and returning to 1 second on a new post, reply, forward, inject or release and on a wake that delivers) and its removed-holder sweep (while mail or injects exist, 30 seconds doubling to 4 minutes while the strand-name set is unchanged).
`deliver_test.go` is a `package creelengine_test` file using exported API only, since an in-package test importing `creelfake` is an import cycle.
`deliver_test.go`, every row on `creelfake`'s clock and delivery: `TestScheduler_Reminders` (a post to a live idle strand reminded once; a reply to a live idle strand with no running worker reminded once; a scheduler started over a pool holding unread mail for a live idle strand reminding it with no new post; the probe interval of a busy receiver, of a dormant receiver with unread mail and of an idle receiver whose reminder is inside its backoff each read off the fake clock's waits as 1, 2, 4, 8 and 8 seconds, back to 1 second after a new post and again after a wake that delivers; a receiver with nothing pending never probed; a busy receiver reminded at its next idle edge; an unanswered reminder turn backs off 5 minutes, doubles to the 1-hour ceiling, and a new message resets it; 7 unread list 5 and count 2; a 100-rune subject with a newline and `»` cut to 80 runes with both replaced; a program mailbox never reminded; an orch and an `orch-2` strand never typed into, one `withheld` line journaled per new message and zero `Idle` calls for either strand; a pause types nothing until lifted while post still stores; a hold mutes another sender's reminder, lets the owner's pass and ends at expiry; a dormant receiver keeps its mail and is reminded once live).
`TestScheduler_Injects` (injects typed before reminders in queue order; `ErrBusy` retried; `ErrNotLanded` journaled unconfirmed and never retyped; the TTL frozen while paused or dormant and running under another sender's hold until it expires untyped; an expired inject never typed; `inject --interrupt` interrupts then types its text first at the next idle; a receiver whose sends stay busy delays no other receiver's delivery; a scripted send error other than the two sentinels, repeated over three probes and then changed, logged at Warn twice through `logcapture` and retried, which makes this test non-parallel; a scripted `Paused` error and, in another row, a scripted `Idle` error, each with a queued inject and unread mail, making zero `Send` calls and logging one Warn line through `logcapture`).
`TestSweep_RemovedHolders` (the sweep waits read off the fake clock as 30 s, 60 s, … up to the 4-minute ceiling while the strand-name set holds, and back to 30 s after a post; mail returned one step after two sweeps and marked with the receiver that ended unread, and in one variant returned to an `orch-2` strand with one `withheld` line naming `creel-notices`, zero `Idle` calls for it and nothing typed, then on toward the sender, then journaled undelivered with its registered waiter answered; a strand removed and re-added between sweeps keeps its mail; a failed strand listing moves nothing and resets no streak; an inject queued for a removed strand journaled expired, its `--wait` answered and absent from the next retention carry).
